{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/questions.json docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/statements-part2.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/questions.json docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/statements-part2.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"question\": \"v1\",\n  \"about\": \"NVDA\",\n  \"kind\": \"asset\",\n  \"asks\": \"What total amount in USD of NVIDIA’s credit-support commitments and minimum-revenue guarantees or backstops to AI labs and cloud partners, including the support for the additional lab’s nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity, will be disclosed in NVIDIA’s FY2027 Form 10-K and related quantified disclosures by the annual report’s publication?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The disclosed amount of guarantees, credit-support commitments and revenue backstops NVIDIA has extended to AI labs and cloud partners (including the credit support for nearly 2 gigawatts of computing capacity for one additional AI lab), versus the equity investments it has made, at NVIDIA's next annual report.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-04-01\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"below 10,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 10,000,000,000 USD to below 25,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 25,000,000,000 USD to below 50,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 50,000,000,000 USD to below 100,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"100,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v2\",\n  \"about\": \"NVDA\",\n  \"kind\": \"asset\",\n  \"asks\": \"How much in purchase obligations and supply commitments will NVIDIA disclose in its FY2027 Form 10-K, as reported in the purchase obligations and contractual commitments disclosures and related notes?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The amount of purchase obligations/supply commitments NVIDIA reports in its contractual obligations and purchase commitment disclosures in the Form 10-K, versus the prior year, given the analyst report that NVIDIA is taking on larger supply commitments.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-04-01\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"below 50,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 50,000,000,000 USD to below 100,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 100,000,000,000 USD to below 150,000,000,000 USD (no reference figure when the question opened)\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 150,000,000,000 USD to below 200,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"200,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v3\",\n  \"about\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n  \"kind\": \"theme\",\n  \"asks\": \"By January 31, 2027, will U.S. authorities authorize Nvidia to sell Blackwell-generation AI chips to China and will Chinese authorities permit those shipments?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether U.S. authorities extend export approval beyond the older H200 to Nvidia's current Blackwell-generation chips for approved Chinese customers, and whether Chinese authorities stop restricting Nvidia chip shipments, so that China data-center revenue can resume; the item reports H200 shipments are already U.S.-permitted while Chinese authorities still restrict them.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"By January 31, 2027, U.S. authorities have authorized sales of Nvidia Blackwell-generation AI chips to China and Chinese authorities permit those shipments.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After September 23, 2026, U.S. export-control authorities formally prohibit Blackwell exports to China, or Chinese authorities formally prohibit Nvidia Blackwell shipments, with the prohibition remaining in force through January 31, 2027. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-23 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v4\",\n  \"about\": \"NVDA\",\n  \"kind\": \"asset\",\n  \"asks\": \"Will NVIDIA disclose in its quarterly results or FY2027 Form 10-K that Vera Rubin made volume customer shipments with first revenue recognition by the end of FY2027 (January 31, 2027)?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether Vera Rubin moves from full production to volume customer shipments and first revenue recognition within NVIDIA's fiscal 2027, as shown in the company's quarterly results and Form 10-K.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"NVIDIA's quarterly results or FY2027 Form 10-K show that Vera Rubin made volume customer shipments with first revenue recognition by January 31, 2027.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After September 23, 2026, NVIDIA formally cancels or abandons the Vera Rubin platform before it makes volume customer shipments. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-23 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v5\",\n  \"about\": \"ai-capex\",\n  \"kind\": \"theme\",\n  \"asks\": \"How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend in total on data centers in calendar 2026, as shown by their Q4/full-year 2026 earnings and capex disclosures?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The big five AI hyperscalers' combined calendar-2026 data center capital expenditure, compared with the nearly $800 billion the article says they will spend this year.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-03-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 775,000,000,000 USD\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 775,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"from 775,000,000,000 USD to below 825,000,000,000 USD\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 775,000,000,000 USD to below 825,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"the big five AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data centers this year\\\")\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"from 825,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"from 825,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"900,000,000,000 USD or more\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"900,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v6\",\n  \"about\": \"NVDA\",\n  \"kind\": \"asset\",\n  \"asks\": \"Will NVIDIA complete (close) its agreed acquisition of Hugging Face, as disclosed in NVIDIA's filings, by March 24, 2028?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether the agreed ~$12.9 billion Hugging Face acquisition is signed and closed (completed) as disclosed in NVIDIA's filings, versus being repriced, delayed past the check date or terminated.\",\n  \"due\": \"2028-03-24\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"NVIDIA completes the Hugging Face acquisition by March 24, 2028, as evidenced by NVIDIA's filings or a completion announcement.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After 2026-09-25, NVIDIA or Hugging Face formally terminates or withdraws the acquisition agreement before it is completed. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-25 and stands on 2028-03-24, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-03-24.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"v7\",\n  \"about\": \"chip-export-controls\",\n  \"kind\": \"theme\",\n  \"asks\": \"Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology (MIIT) formally approve purchases of Nvidia's RTX Pro 5500 by Alibaba, ByteDance, or other Chinese firms by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Whether MIIT moves from signaling intent and collecting purchase plans to actually approving Alibaba's, ByteDance's and other Chinese firms' purchases of the RTX Pro 5500 (versus blocking, delaying or capping quantities), so that Nvidia can ship the product into China and book related revenue.\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   {\n    \"answer\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"MIIT formally approves by January 31, 2027, a purchase of RTX Pro 5500 chips by Alibaba, ByteDance, or another Chinese firm.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Ruled out\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"After September 27, 2026, MIIT formally rejects all RTX Pro 5500 purchase plans from Alibaba, ByteDance, and other Chinese firms, or formally prohibits those firms from purchasing the chips. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-09-27 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"answer\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Still open\",\n    \"holds_when\": \"Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n   }\n  ]\n }\n][\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e96\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Microsoft Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com (article, no byline)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article expects Microsoft to become one of Nscale's most important customers, implying additional take-or-pay demand for the AI cloud capacity NVIDIA equips.\",\n  \"quote\": \"while Microsoft Corporation (NASDAQ: MSFT ) is expected to become one of Nscale's most important customers\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e97\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Apple\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"gurufocus.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Apple demonstrated four connected Mac Studios running a trillion-parameter AI model to fix a coding bug, pitching on-premises Macs as a way for businesses with steady workloads or sensitive data to run demanding models without paying a cloud bill for every token — a competitive pitch at the smaller end of the AI market where NVIDIA sells data-center GPUs for inference.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia ( NASDAQ:NVDA ), the AI chip and data center leader, faces a challenge at the smaller end of the AI market: Apple ( NASDAQ:AAPL ) is pitching Macs that run demanding models in an office, without a cloud bill for every token. … Apple demonstrated four connected Mac Studios running a trillion-parameter model to fix a coding bug. The pitch is simple: buy the machines once, then keep using them. That could appeal to businesses with steady workloads or sensitive data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e98\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"gurufocus.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported that in its latest quarter data centers generated $89 billion of its $96.2 billion in total revenue, or roughly 92.5%, showing how concentrated the company's revenue is in data-center AI chips.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia's latest quarter puts the scale of the contest in perspective: data centers generated $89 billion of its $96.2 billion in revenue, or roughly 92.5%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e99\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-21\",\n  \"summary\": \"On September 21, 2026, NVIDIA Corporation introduced its DSX Ready program and named Tesla, Inc. among qualified battery-energy-storage suppliers and Vertiv Holdings Co among qualified cooling suppliers for its AI data-center 'AI-factory' compatibility standard; the article describes the program as a published compatibility layer for the physical AI factory intended to shorten developers' design work and potentially increase Nvidia's influence over what is specified around its racks.\",\n  \"quote\": \"On September 21, the company introduced its DSX Ready program and named Tesla, Inc. (NASDAQ: TSLA ) among qualified battery-energy-storage suppliers and Vertiv Holdings Co (NYSE: VRT ) among qualified cooling suppliers. NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) is effectively publishing a compatibility layer for the physical AI factory, which can shorten design work for developers while potentially increasing Nvidia's influence over what gets specified around its racks.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e100\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-21\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA qualified Vertiv Holdings Co's 2.3-megawatt CoolChip coolant distribution unit for its DSX Ready program, per the article; the article says higher rack density raises cooling content per megawatt but notes that qualification alone does not guarantee project wins.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Vertiv Holdings Co (NYSE:VRT) has the most direct operating exposure because Nvidia qualified its 2.3-megawatt CoolChip coolant distribution unit for the program. … The counterweight is expectations. Vertiv has already rerated around AI demand, so qualification matters most if it converts into orders and margins rather than becoming a logo on a standards page.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e101\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA stated that its DSX Ready qualification program does not replace site-level engineering or imply site-level stability, i.e. supplier qualification under the program is not a guarantee of project wins or of site-level operational stability.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia itself says DSX Ready does not replace site-level engineering or imply site-level stability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e102\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Fool.com opinion column (unnamed contributor)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia estimates that global data center capital expenditures will rise to between $3 trillion and $4 trillion by 2030, an estimate cited in a Fool.com opinion column on 23 September 2026.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia estimates that global data center capital expenditures will rise to between $3 trillion and $4 trillion by 2030.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e103\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Fool.com opinion column (unnamed contributor)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Fool.com opinion column (unnamed contributor)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"The Fool.com opinion column states that the big five AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data centers in 2026, offered as the basis for continued growth in AI computing demand.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Considering the big five AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data centers this year, that's huge growth still to come.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e104\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia, in its quarterly results reported in the month before this 23 September 2026 Barchart article, posted what the article calls a market-beating fiscal Q2 and issued guidance for about 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Last month, Nvidia posted a market-beating Q2 and issued bullish guidance for about 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, which makes its current P/E multiple of about 24x appear rather attractive.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e105\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Amazon.com (AMZN)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article cites a recent deal between Nvidia and Amazon (AMZN) involving 2 million GPUs, described as one reason NVDA remains a compelling long-term holding in 2026; no deal value or timing is given.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The recent deal with Amazon (AMZN) involving 2 million GPUs and billions being spent on buybacks and dividend payments make NVDA an even more compelling long-term holding in 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e106\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (management; CFO Colette Kress)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com (article author)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"On NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said customer forecasts point to the company's growth doubling next year, but that NVIDIA expects to grow approximately 70% because it is supply-constrained; NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 second-quarter report forecast 70% sales growth for fiscal 2028, and leadership said sales could double in fiscal 2028 if constraints on the supply of commodities needed for its hardware were overcome.\",\n  \"quote\": \"In its fiscal 2027 second-quarter report, Management forecast that in fiscal 2028, its sales will rise by 70%, thanks to continued demand for AI chips. … But what's really interesting is that Nvidia leadership said it could double its sales in fiscal 2028 if it were able to overcome the constraints on the supply of commodities needed to produce its hardware. … On Nvidia's second-quarter fiscal 2027 earnings call , Nvidia CFO Colette Kress said: … Incredibly, we are seeing demand acceleration even at our scale. Customer forecasts point to our growth doubling next year. However, as I mentioned earlier, we expect to grow approximately 70% as we are supply-constrained.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e107\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"S&P Global\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com (article author)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"S&P Global recently forecast that technology companies will spend an estimated $1.3 trillion on AI 'next year' — i.e. calendar 2027, as reported in a 23 September 2026 article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"S&P Global recently forecast that tech companies will spend an estimated $1.3 trillion on AI next year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e108\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Micron Technology (as reported)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com (article author)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article reports that Micron Technology's memory chips are in severe shortage, with demand far outpacing supply, which has driven skyrocketing memory prices, higher margins for Micron and global supply constraints.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For example, Micron Technology 's memory chips are having a significant problem, with demand far outpacing supply. That's led to skyrocketing memory prices, higher margins for Micron, and global supply constraints.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e109\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (CEO Jensen Huang)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com (article author)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"On the fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call, NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said 'the amount of compute necessary is just extraordinary' because AI agents use between 15 and 100 times as much compute as would be required with a human guiding the work.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said on the earnings call that \\\"the amount of compute necessary is just extraordinary\\\" because AI agents use between 15 and 100 times as much compute as would be required with a human guiding the work.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e110\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%; Data Center revenue was $89.023 billion, according to the article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Q2 fiscal 2027 delivered revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%. Data Center revenue hit $89.023 billion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e111\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided third-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue to $108 billion, a guidance the article says excludes China Data Center compute revenue, cited as geopolitical uncertainty.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Management guided Q3 to $108 billion. … Q3 guidance excludes China Data Center compute revenue citing geopolitical uncertainty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e112\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"24/7 Wall St.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article expects NVIDIA's gross margin to bottom at 71% to 72% in Q4 on memory cost inflation and to recover to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale (the item says 'Q4' without naming the fiscal year; context is fiscal 2027).\",\n  \"quote\": \"Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e113\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article lists supply commitments of $279 billion among NVIDIA's real risks.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e114\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article lists guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion among NVIDIA's real risks.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e115\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article reports that NVIDIA's days sales outstanding (DSO) is extending to 60 days, listing it among the company's real risks.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e116\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (Jensen Huang)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Jensen Huang told investors that NVIDIA can supply only 70% of demand, and the article states fiscal 2028 growth is pegged at approximately 70%.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Jensen Huang told investors NVIDIA can supply only 70% of demand, with fiscal 2028 growth pegged at approximately 70%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e117\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"24/7 Wall St.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article states that Vera Rubin raises platform value per gigawatt to $40 billion from Blackwell's $25 billion.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Vera Rubin ramps platform value per gigawatt from Blackwell's $25 billion to $40 billion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e118\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article cites more than $500 billion in third-party AI infrastructure capital being mobilized through NVIDIA partners as one of three catalysts behind its buy call.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Three catalysts drive the call: the Vera Rubin production ramp, more than $500 billion in third-party AI infrastructure capital being mobilized through NVIDIA partners, and the opening chapter of physical AI across robotics and autonomous vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e119\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"24/7 Wall St.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article states hyperscaler capex is expected to reach nearly 800 billion in 2026 and 1.3 trillion in 2027.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Hyperscaler capex is expected to reach nearly 800 billion in 2026 and 1.3 trillion in 2027, a wave that also pulls in the power, cooling, and networking suppliers we profiled in a free report on seven AI infrastructure names that aren't chipmakers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e120\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Advanced Micro Devices (AMD)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Advanced Micro Devices posted second-quarter fiscal 2026 revenue of $11.536 billion, up 50.11%, with Data Center revenue up 107%, according to the article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Advanced Micro Devices ( NASDAQ:AMD ) posted Q2 fiscal 2026 revenue of $11.536 billion, up 50.11%, with Data Center up 107%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e121\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Broadcom (AVGO)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"24/7 Wall St. (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Broadcom competes in custom AI ASICs and networking; its third-quarter fiscal 2026 revenue reached $29.591 billion, up 85.5%, with AI semiconductor revenue of $16.70 billion growing 221% year over year, according to the article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Broadcom ( NASDAQ:AVGO ) competes in custom AI ASICs and networking. Q3 fiscal 2026 revenue reached $29.591 billion, up 85.5%, with AI semiconductor revenue of $16.70 billion growing 221% year over year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e122\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"uk.finance.yahoo.com (Yahoo Finance UK)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's second-quarter net income rose 126% year-on-year to $59.7bn, according to the Yahoo Finance UK article, which notes earnings grew roughly 4.5 times faster than the share price over the same comparison.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Second-quarter net income rocketed 126% to $59.7bn year-on-year, around 4.5 times faster than the stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e123\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Einride AB\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-21\",\n  \"summary\": \"On 21 September 2026, autonomous-freight operator Einride AB (NASDAQ: ENRD) announced a strategic collaboration with NVIDIA around NVIDIA's DRIVE Hyperion autonomous-driving compute platform, according to this 23 September 2026 article; no financial terms, volumes or contract value were disclosed, and the article notes Einride's separate fleet plan (about 500 Tesla Semis, part of a roughly 1,500–2,000-vehicle fleet by 2028) is distinct from the NVIDIA tie-up.\",\n  \"quote\": \"On September 21, the autonomous-freight operator announced a strategic collaboration with NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) around DRIVE Hyperion, while its separate fleet plan calls for hundreds of Tesla, Inc. (NASDAQ: TSLA ) Semis. … Nvidia's Hyperion platform gives Einride a standardized path for perception and autonomous-driving compute.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e124\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA mentioned warm-water cooling technology during a keynote address, and investors read the remark as a threat to SPX Technologies' air-cooled cooling towers; the article ties that reading to the selloff that has dragged SPX shares from above $230 toward their 52-week low. The item gives no date, product name or technical detail for the NVIDIA remark.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The selloff that has dragged the stock from above $230 down toward its 52-week low has a specific, nameable cause. … Nvidia mentioned warm-water cooling technology during a keynote, and investors immediately read that as a threat to SPX's air-cooled towers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e125\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"SPX Technologies, Inc.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"SPX Technologies lifted its data center capacity expectations to $1.1 billion from $750 million — a 47% increase — which the article says reflects real customer commitments rather than forward-looking optimism; the raise was disclosed alongside its Q2 2026 results (revenue of $679 million, adjusted EPS of $2.02 versus a $1.85 estimate, and full-year adjusted EPS guidance raised to $8.20–$8.60).\",\n  \"quote\": \"The company also lifted its data center capacity expectations to $1.1B from $750M, a 47% increase that reflects real customer commitments rather than forward-looking optimism.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e126\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Wall Street consensus (analysts)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Jeremy Bowman, Motley Fool\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Motley Fool contributor Jeremy Bowman reports that Wall Street expects Nvidia to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year, contrasting that pace with the S&P 500's slower growth.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Because of its central position in the AI boom, Nvidia is growing much faster than the S&P 500. Wall Street expects the company to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e127\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Wall Street consensus (analysts)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Jeremy Bowman, Motley Fool\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Motley Fool contributor Jeremy Bowman reports that Nvidia is expected by consensus to earn earnings per share of $15.68 in fiscal 2028, which ends in January of that year.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For fiscal 2028, which ends in January of that year, Nvidia is expected to have earnings per share of $15.68.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e128\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Daniel Sparks, fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter (quarter ended July 26, 2026) revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and an acceleration from the previous quarter, with the data center business contributing all but about $7 billion of the total; net income rose 126% year over year to $59.7 billion.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second quarter (ended July 26) was another exceptional one. Revenue grew 106% year over year to $96.2 billion, an acceleration from the previous quarter, and the data center business contributed all but about $7 billion of the total. Profit kept up. Net income rose 126% year over year, to $59.7 billion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e129\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Daniel Sparks, fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia management guided revenue for the current quarter (fiscal Q3 2027) to $108.0 billion, described in the item as another step up from fiscal Q2's $96.2 billion.\",\n  \"quote\": \"And management guided for another step up in this quarter (fiscal Q3): $108.0 billion of revenue.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e130\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Nvidia (Colette Kress, CFO)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Daniel Sparks, fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"On Nvidia's earnings call in late August 2026, chief financial officer Colette Kress guided fiscal 2028 revenue growth of approximately 70%, characterising the outlook as supply-constrained.\",\n  \"quote\": \"On the company's earnings call in late August, chief financial officer Colette Kress went a whole year further. … \\\"We expect to grow revenue by approximately 70% in fiscal 2028,\\\" Kress said. \\\"This is a supply-constrained outlook.\\\"\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e131\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Advanced Micro Devices (AMD)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Daniel Sparks, fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"AMD reported second-quarter 2026 revenue of a record $11.5 billion, up 50% from a year earlier; its data center segment, which sells EPYC server processors and Instinct GPUs into the same AI build-out Nvidia serves, more than doubled year over year to $6.7 billion, or 58% of company revenue.\",\n  \"quote\": \"AMD's rally has real results behind it. Revenue for the second quarter of 2026 hit a record $11.5 billion, up 50% from a year ago. … And the data center segment, which sells EPYC server processors and Instinct graphics processing units into the same AI build-out Nvidia serves, more than doubled year over year, totaling $6.7 billion (58% of the company's revenue).\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e132\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Advanced Micro Devices (AMD)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Daniel Sparks, fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"AMD guided third-quarter 2026 revenue to around $13 billion, which the item says implies about 41% year-over-year growth.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Guidance for the third quarter of 2026 is around $13 billion, which implies about 41% year-over-year growth.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e133\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) — Lisa Su, CEO\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Daniel Sparks, fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"AMD chief executive Lisa Su told analysts on the company's August 2026 earnings call that AMD now expects data center segment revenue to more than double year over year in 2027.\",\n  \"quote\": \"And CEO Lisa Su told analysts on the company's August earnings call that the bigger move happens next year. … \\\"[W]e now expect data center segment revenue to more than double year-over-year in 2027,\\\" Su said.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e134\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's reported Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with Q3 fiscal 2027 revenue guided to $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%; the article uses this to argue the insider sales reflect portfolio moves, not a business warning.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with a Q3 guide of $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%. … Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year to $96B, making the director's trim a portfolio move, not a business warning.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e135\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance (finance.yahoo.com); Jensen Huang quoted\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in the Frontier AI Labs and helped arrange over $500 billion of third-party capital with six infrastructure providers, and CEO Jensen Huang acknowledged the scale of that support while saying the company does not see it as 'circular financing'.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The louder concern is circular financing. NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in the Frontier AI Labs and helped arrange over $500 billion of third-party capital with six infrastructure providers. CEO Jensen Huang addressed the skepticism directly: \\\"We recognize the scale of this support, and we know some will call this circular financing. We see it differently.\\\"\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e136\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance (finance.yahoo.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article reports that NVIDIA's supply commitments have surged to $279 billion and its guarantee obligations are capped at $108.5 billion, describing both as real balance-sheet exposures if demand slips.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Bear: the sale is large, outside a prearranged plan, and arrives as the market questions whether the spending cycle is self-funded. Supply commitments surged to $279 billion, and guarantee obligations are capped at $108.5 billion. Those are real balance-sheet exposures if demand slips.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e137\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported $96.2 billion in revenue for its fiscal second quarter, up 106% from the same period a year earlier, and a 75% gross margin.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year. … The company also produced a 75% gross margin\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e138\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year.\",\n  \"quote\": \"management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e139\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided to $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e140\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article reports that NVIDIA's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months, with receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July.\",\n  \"quote\": \"However, a closer look at the company's balance sheet shows that Nvidia's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months. … A big part of that is the company's receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e141\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article calculates that NVIDIA's days sales outstanding rose from 45 to 60 days in one quarter, which it says means customers are taking longer to pay.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia's DSO went from 45 to 60 days in one quarter. Customers are taking longer to pay.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e142\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA said it extended payment terms on large orders from certain customers, which the article cites as the reason for the rise in days sales outstanding.\",\n  \"quote\": \"To be fair, Nvidia told us why. The company extended payment terms on large orders from certain customers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e143\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of data center lease obligations for OpenAI.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For example, Nvidia agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of data center lease obligations for OpenAI.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e144\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has formed partnerships to raise over $500 billion of outside capital for AI infrastructure, according to the article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"It has formed partnerships to raise over $500 billion of outside capital for AI infrastructure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e145\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"IonQ\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"IonQ announced it will deploy its Superion 256 quantum computer on-premise at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center. The article describes the deployment as tying IonQ's Superion 256 hardware to CUDA Q and GB200 NVL72 infrastructure in an on-premise environment — a partner integration with NVIDIA's Blackwell-generation systems and quantum software platform; no shipment date, order value or scale of NVIDIA benefit is given.\",\n  \"quote\": \"IonQ recently announced it will deploy its Superion 256 quantum computer on-premise at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, while also unveiling an end-to-end real-time quantum error correction decoder that runs on a single off-the-shelf CPU with minimal computational delay. … The NVIDIA Accelerated Quantum Research Center deployment stands out as the most relevant announcement here, because it ties IonQ's Superion 256 hardware to CUDA Q and GB200 NVL72 infrastructure in a real on premise environment.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e146\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Apple\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"gurufocus.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Apple is making an unusually aggressive push into enterprise artificial intelligence, pitching its newest high-end Macs — upgraded Mac mini and Mac Studio systems — as an alternative to the expensive cloud computing capacity that has helped Nvidia and Microsoft dominate the AI boom, arguing businesses can run AI workloads locally rather than paying cloud providers for tokens. The item gives no adoption, order or spending figures for the effort.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Apple ( NASDAQ:AAPL ) is making an unusually aggressive push into enterprise artificial intelligence , pitching its newest high-end Macs as an alternative to the expensive cloud infrastructure that has helped Nvidia ( NASDAQ:NVDA ) and Microsoft ( NASDAQ:MSFT ) dominate the AI boom. … Its upgraded Mac mini and Mac Studio systems are aimed at tasks including software development and complex business workflows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e147\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"IonQ\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Howard Smith (Motley Fool)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"IonQ announced that its Superion 256 trapped-ion quantum system will be installed in Nvidia's accelerated quantum research center, where it will run as a niche processing system alongside Nvidia GPU clusters — a deployment IonQ disclosed alongside its decoder breakthrough.\",\n  \"quote\": \"In addition to that news, IonQ announced a potentially important step toward commercializing its quantum systems. Its Superion 256 system will be installed in Nvidia's accelerated quantum research center to run as a niche processing system alongside Nvidia GPU (graphics processing unit) clusters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e148\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"U.S. government (Washington)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article reports that Washington has for years restricted China's access to Nvidia's most advanced AI chips and to the equipment used to make them, on the bet that limiting computing power would keep Chinese AI a generation behind; the restriction is described as in force as of the 23 September 2026 article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Washington has for years restricted China's access to Nvidia's most advanced AI chips and the equipment to make them, betting that starving computing power would keep Chinese AI a generation behind.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e149\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"U.S. Trade Representative Jamieson Greer\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"During the September 2026 Trump–Xi state visit, the article said neither side appeared ready to put chip export controls on the table; Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and U.S. Trade Representative Jamieson Greer met Vice Premier He Lifeng in New York over the weekend and set up a formal AI channel for incident warnings, and Greer said explicitly that export controls on advanced chips and chipmaking equipment were not on the agenda.\",\n  \"quote\": \"As Trump hosts Xi for a multi-day state visit, neither side appears ready to put chip export controls on the table. … Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and U.S. Trade Representative Jamieson Greer met Vice Premier He Lifeng in New York over the weekend and set up a formal AI channel for incident warnings. But Greer said explicitly that export controls on advanced chips and chipmaking equipment were not on the agenda.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e150\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Huawei\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Huawei said at its annual Huawei Connect conference, the week before the 23 September 2026 article, that its Ascent 960DT AI chip will ship in the first quarter of 2027, three quarters ahead of its original schedule.\",\n  \"quote\": \"At its annual Huawei Connect conference last week, Huawei said its Ascent 960DT will ship in the first quarter of 2027 , three quarters ahead of its original schedule.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e151\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Alibaba (chip unit)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"At the Apsara Conference in Hangzhou on the Tuesday before the 23 September 2026 article, Alibaba's chip unit unveiled the Zhenwu V900 AI chip, which it says triples the performance of its predecessor and will go on sale in early 2027.\",\n  \"quote\": \"At the Apsara Conference in Hangzhou on Tuesday, Alibaba's chip unit unveiled the Zhenwu V900 chip , which triples the performance of its predecessor and will go on sale in early 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e152\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article reports that Huawei's latest SuperPoD computing architecture links far fewer processors than originally planned, and that each Huawei chip still delivers roughly half the compute of Nvidia's chips.\",\n  \"quote\": \"But the approach has limits. Huawei's latest SuperPoD computing architecture links far fewer processors than originally planned, and each chip still delivers roughly half the compute of Nvidia's.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e153\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Huawei (Chairman Eric Xu)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Huawei Chairman Eric Xu acknowledged that Huawei may not be able to make enough AI chips to meet Chinese domestic demand, and that Chinese AI developers may not be advanced enough to experience rogue safety risks, as reported in the 23 September 2026 article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Chairman Eric Xu acknowledged that Huawei may not be able to make enough chips to meet domestic demand, and that Chinese AI developers may not be advanced enough to experience rogue safety risks.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e154\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Chris Miller (Tufts University)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Chris Miller, a Tufts University professor and author of 'Chip War', said Chinese firms remain substantially short of the chips needed to train and deploy advanced models and rely heavily on smuggling chips or gaining access to data centers outside China, concluding that China is still highly dependent on the U.S. for advanced chips.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Chinese firms remain substantially short of the chips needed to train and deploy advanced models, and rely heavily on smuggling chips or gaining access to data centers outside China, Miller said. \\\"China is still highly dependent on the U.S. for advanced chips.\\\"\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e155\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"DeepSeek\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"CNBC\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"DeepSeek, the AI startup whose low-cost model rattled global markets the previous year, reportedly lined up the largest known cluster of Huawei chips built to date, according to the article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"DeepSeek, the startup whose low-cost model rattled global markets last year, reportedly lined up the largest known cluster of Huawei chips built to date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e156\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"IonQ\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"barchart.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"IonQ announced on 23 September 2026 a partnership with Nvidia to deploy IonQ's trapped-ion quantum computer at Nvidia's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, aligning IonQ's next-generation trapped-ion architecture with Nvidia's CUDA-Q open platform and H200 GPUs so researchers can run hybrid classical-quantum workflows. The item reports the announcement as news; no contract value, capacity or shipment volume is given.\",\n  \"quote\": \"IonQ (IONQ) shares inched higher on Sept. 23 after announcing a landmark partnership with Nvidia (NVDA) to deploy its quantum computer at the AI titan's Accelerated Quantum Research Center. … The deal aligns IonQ's trapped-ion hardware with Nvidia's CUDA-Q platform, advancing hybrid classical-quantum supercomputing. … Integrating IonQ's next-generation trapped-ion architecture with Nvidia's CUDA-Q open platform and H200 GPUs allows researchers to run accelerated hybrid workflows and generative AI circuit optimization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e157\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (Marcio Gomes, Enterprise Sales Director for Latin America)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Diego Valverde, mexicobusiness.news, reporting remarks by Marcio Gomes of NVIDIA\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA Enterprise Sales Director for Latin America Marcio Gomes said that 82 Mexican startups are participating in NVIDIA Inception, the chipmaker's free global program that gives AI startups technical training, developer tools, preferred pricing on selected hardware and software, cloud credits and investor introductions, with no application or membership fees and no equity requirements. The item gives no fee revenue, order, capacity or spending figure tied to the program and no date for the count.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Mexico has 82 startups participating in NVIDIA Inception, the chipmaker’s global program designed to support artificial intelligence companies through technical resources, business guidance, and connections to investors. The figure, confirmed by Marcio Gomes, Enterprise Sales Director for Latin America, NVIDIA, highlights the growing presence of AI-focused businesses within Mexico’s technology ecosystem.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e158\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Skild AI (with Nvidia and Foxconn)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"aibusiness.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Nvidia-backed startup Skild AI, together with Nvidia and contract manufacturer Foxconn, recently began using Skild's 'Skild Brain' omni-bodied foundation model on dual-arm robots at an Nvidia factory in Houston to assemble Nvidia Blackwell GPU systems — a deployment the article presents as under way, built on Nvidia AI infrastructure (Cosmos, Isaac Lab, Isaac Sim and Omniverse) for data generation, training, simulation and deployment.\",\n  \"quote\": \"The technology is already being deployed at an Nvidia factory in Houston, where Skild, Nvidia and contract electronics manufacturing giant Foxconn recently began using the Skild Brain omni-bodied foundation model on dual-arm robots to assemble Nvidia Blackwell GPU systems. … S1 was built on Nvidia AI infrastructure, using Cosmos, Isaac Lab, Isaac Sim and Omniverse across data generation, training, simulation and deployment.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e159\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Skild AI\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"aibusiness.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Skild AI, the Nvidia-backed developer of a general-purpose robot foundation model, said it reached a $100 million annual revenue run rate earlier in September 2026, only 10 months after its first commercial deployment; the company cited this as evidence that robot foundation models are moving beyond demos into real work.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Skild reached a $100 million annual revenue run rate earlier this month, just 10 months after its first commercial deployment. This, according to the company, is evidence that robot foundation models are moving beyond demos and into real work.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e160\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"IonQ\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"tradingview.com (Stocktwits article)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"IonQ said on Wednesday (23 September 2026) that its Superion 256 quantum system is scheduled to be installed next year at Nvidia's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, where it will be linked directly to an Nvidia GB200 NVL72 system, using Nvidia's NVQLink technology and CUDA-Q platform to connect the quantum processor to Nvidia's accelerated computing infrastructure; the joint research program will focus on hybrid quantum-classical software and large-scale system prototypes. IonQ described the system as the first on-premises quantum processor deployed at the center. This is a stated deployment plan for 2027, not a confirmed order, delivery or revenue for Nvidia.\",\n  \"quote\": \"IonQ (IONQ) shares jumped in pre-market trade on Wednesday after the company said it successfully tested its first real-time quantum error decoder and announced that its Superion 256 system will become the first on-premises quantum processor deployed at Nvidia’s Accelerated Quantum Research Center. … IonQ said on Wednesday that its Superion 256 will be installed at Nvidia’s Accelerated Quantum Research Center next year, where it will be linked directly to an Nvidia GB200 NVL72 system. … The companies will use Nvidia’s NVQLink technology and CUDA-Q platform to connect the quantum processor with Nvidia’s accelerated computing infrastructure. The research program will focus on hybrid quantum-classical software and large-scale system prototypes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e161\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"IonQ\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"quantumcomputingreport.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"IonQ announced that its sixth-generation Superion 256 trapped-ion quantum processing unit (QPU) will be the first on-premise quantum computer installed at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC), scheduled for installation in 2027 alongside IonQ's first commercial deliveries. The deployment establishes a direct hardware interconnect between IonQ's 256-qubit system and an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 accelerated computing rack via NVIDIA NVQLink, with hybrid quantum-classical workloads on the unified system orchestrated by NVIDIA's open-source CUDA-Q software platform.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Trapped-ion quantum hardware developer IonQ (NYSE: IONQ) has announced that its sixth-generation Superion 256 quantum processing unit (QPU) will serve as the first on-premise quantum computer installed at the NVIDIA Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC) . Scheduled for installation in 2027 alongside first commercial deliveries, the deployment establishes a direct hardware interconnect between IonQ’s 256-qubit system and an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 accelerated computing rack via NVIDIA NVQLink . Hybrid quantum-classical workloads across the unified system will be orchestrated by the open-source NVIDIA CUDA-Q software platform.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e162\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"The Motley Fool (Keithen Drury)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"On NVIDIA's most recent earnings call, the company said data center capital expenditures by the big five AI hyperscalers will approach $800 billion this year (2026) and are estimated to rise to $1.3 trillion next year (2027), as reported by The Motley Fool.\",\n  \"quote\": \"During its most recent earnings call, Nvidia noted that this year's data center capital expenditures from the big five AI hyperscalers will approach $800 billion. Next year, that figure is estimated to rise to $1.3 trillion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e163\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"The Motley Fool (Keithen Drury)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA said it sees global annual data center capital expenditures increasing to $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030, a long-dated demand forecast quoted by The Motley Fool.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Ultimately, Nvidia sees global annual data center capital expenditures increasing to $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e164\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (TSMC)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"The Motley Fool (Keithen Drury)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"TSMC announced an additional $100 billion investment in its Arizona production facilities during Q2, an expansion reported by The Motley Fool as a sign the foundry expects more demand requiring additional production capacity; the item does not state the build-out schedule or any allocation of that capacity to NVIDIA.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Furthermore, TSMC announced an additional $100 billion investment in its Arizona production facilities during Q2, so clearly it sees more demand coming that requires increased production capacity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e165\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"said_by\": \"IonQ\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"IonQ press release, carried by thequantuminsider.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-23\",\n  \"summary\": \"IonQ announced it will make the first on-premise quantum computing deployment at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC), installing an IonQ Superion 256 system directly linked to an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 system via NVIDIA NVQLink, with workloads orchestrated by the open NVIDIA CUDA-Q platform; the partners will research quantum-GPU system design, hybrid software and applications in finance, materials science and drug discovery, with installation scheduled for 2027.\",\n  \"quote\": \"IonQ plans to install a Superion 256 quantum computer at NVIDIA’s Accelerated Quantum Research Center, making it the center’s first on-premise quantum computing deployment. … The system will connect directly to an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 platform through NVQLink and use CUDA-Q to coordinate hybrid quantum-classical workloads. … The partners will research quantum-GPU system design, hybrid software and applications in finance, materials science and drug discovery, with installation scheduled for 2027. … Today, IonQ (NYSE: IONQ) announced that it will be the first on-premise quantum computing deployment at the NVIDIA Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC). … As part of the partnership, an IonQ Superion 256 system will be installed at the NVAQC and directly linked with an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 system via NVIDIA NVQLink , with workloads orchestrated by the open NVIDIA CUDA-Q platform.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e166\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported second-quarter fiscal 2027 (quarter ended 26 July 2026) revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, of which $89 billion — roughly 92.5% of total revenue — came from the data center segment. Net income was $59.68 billion, up 126%, and earnings per share were $2.46, up 128%. Operating expenses were $8.4 billion for the quarter and gross margin was 75%.\",\n  \"quote\": \"What stands out in Nvidia's most recent earnings report is that the company is still growing at a triple-digit rate. Revenue in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 (ending July 26, 2026) was $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year ago. Of that, $89 billion, or roughly 92.5% of the company's total revenue, came from its data center segment. … Net income was $59.68 billion, up 126% from a year ago, and earnings per share of $2.46 were up 128% from last year. Nvidia is very profitable -- its operating expenses totaled only $8.4 billion for the quarter, and its gross margin was an impressive 75%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e167\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (CEO Jensen Huang)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the company is the only one that creates and builds an entire AI factory platform, and that the part of the market made up of sovereign AI, regional AIs, neoclouds, AI start-ups and enterprises represents about half of NVIDIA's business and is growing 100% a year.\",\n  \"quote\": \"\\\"We're the only company in the world that creates and builds, offers an entire AI factory platform, a full-stack system. And customers can still mix and match,\\\" CEO Jensen Huang said. \\\"However, most companies just don't have the skills to do that or desire to do that. And so, there's an entire part of the market that we experience growth. There's sovereign AI, there're regional AIs, there're neoclouds, there're AI start-ups, there're enterprises, where we're seeing -- which represents about half of our business, and that's growing 100% a year.\\\"\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e168\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (CFO Colette Kress)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said the Vera Rubin architecture is now in full production and that Vera Rubin and the full-stack AI platform have expanded the company's total addressable market to $40 billion per gigawatt, from a range of $18 billion to $25 billion per gigawatt for Blackwell.\",\n  \"quote\": \"CFO Colette Kress said the Vera Rubin -- now in full production -- and full-stack AI platform has expanded the company's total addressable market from a range of $18 billion to $25 billion per gigawatt from Blackwell to $40 billion from Vera Rubin.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e169\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (CEO Jensen Huang)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang, speaking to reporters the week before the article's 24 September 2026 publication while in Scotland, suggested NVIDIA would double its chip sales in the coming year.\",\n  \"quote\": \"And speaking to reporters last week while in Scotland, Huang suggested that Nvidia would double its chip sales in the coming year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e170\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Analyst consensus (as reported by fool.com)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The consensus revenue estimate for NVIDIA's next quarterly report (expected in late November) is $109.0 billion, up 91.2% from the previous year, with similar performance expected for the following year after the Vera Rubin ramp-up, according to the article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia is expected to report another strong quarter when it next reports earnings (likely in late November), with the consensus revenue estimate of $109.0 billion, up 91.2% from the previous year. And more of the same is expected for next year, following the Vera Rubin ramp-up.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e171\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA (CEO Jensen Huang)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang has reiterated a prediction he first made last year that AI infrastructure spending would reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\",\n  \"quote\": \"That's one of the reasons why Huang has been so confident in his prediction -- which he made last year and recently reiterated -- that AI infrastructure spending would reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e172\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA Corporation generated $96.2 billion of quarterly revenue (the quarter is not named in the item), up 106%, with Data Center revenue rising 117% to $89.0 billion and gross margin at 75%.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) generated $96.2 billion of quarterly revenue, up 106%, with Data Center revenue rising 117% to $89.0 billion and gross margin at 75%.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e173\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's third-quarter revenue outlook is $108 billion.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Its third-quarter revenue outlook is $108 billion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e174\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Advanced Micro Devices reported second-quarter revenue of $11.5 billion, up 50% year over year, while Data Center revenue more than doubled to $6.7 billion; non-GAAP gross margin reached 56%.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) reported second-quarter revenue of $11.5 billion, up 50% year over year, while Data Center revenue more than doubled to $6.7 billion. Non-GAAP gross margin reached 56%\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e175\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"AMD management expects third-quarter revenue of about $13 billion, which the article said implied roughly 41% growth.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Non-GAAP gross margin reached 56%, and management expects third-quarter revenue of about $13 billion, implying roughly 41% growth.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e176\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Anthropic\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"finance.yahoo.com\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"Anthropic has agreed to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of AMD MI450-series systems, with the first gigawatt expected to begin deployment in the first half of 2027.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Anthropic has agreed to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of MI450-series systems, with the first gigawatt expected to begin deployment in the first half of 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e177\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"IonQ\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"IonQ announced that it will deploy its Superion 256 quantum computer as the first on-premise system at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, directly linking the quantum hardware to NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 infrastructure through NVQLink and CUDA-Q for hybrid AI and quantum workloads; the deployment is planned, with no date given.\",\n  \"quote\": \"In recent days, IonQ announced it will deploy its Superion 256 quantum computer as the first on‑premise system at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, directly linking quantum hardware to NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 infrastructure via NVQLink and CUDA‑Q for hybrid AI and quantum workloads.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e178\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"AI Energy Management Alliance (Emerald AI and Google)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article highlights the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance with Emerald AI and Google and says that if AI data centers can become more grid-friendly and flex their power use, it may help ease one of NVIDIA's key risks around data center energy constraints and policy pushback.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Among the recent announcements, the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance with Emerald AI and Google stands out here. If AI data centers can become more \\\"grid friendly\\\" and flex their power use, that may help ease one of NVIDIA's key risks around data center energy constraints and policy pushback, supporting the thesis that AI infrastructure build outs can continue to scale from here.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e179\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Yahoo Finance (NVIDIA narrative)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article's NVIDIA investment narrative projects $714.0 billion of revenue and $392.6 billion of earnings by 2029, requiring 41.2% yearly revenue growth and about a $233.0 billion earnings increase from $159.6 billion today.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA's narrative projects $714.0 billion revenue and $392.6 billion earnings by 2029. This requires 41.2% yearly revenue growth and about a $233.0 billion earnings increase from $159.6 billion today.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e180\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Unnamed optimistic analysts\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Yahoo Finance\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"The article states that some of the most optimistic, unnamed analysts already expected NVIDIA's earnings to climb toward about US$666.5 billion by 2029.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Some of the most optimistic analysts already expected NVIDIA's earnings to climb toward about US$666.5 billion by 2029\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e181\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Super Micro Computer\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"GuruFocus (gurufocus.com)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"summary\": \"Super Micro Computer moved into commercial shipments of servers built around NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform, shipping Vera Rubin NVL72 racks through its Data Center Building Block Solutions that combine computing hardware with liquid cooling, networking, storage and power components; each rack design uses 72 Rubin GPUs and 36 Vera CPUs, according to a GuruFocus report published 24 September 2026.\",\n  \"quote\": \"the server maker moved into commercial shipments of systems built around NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform, adding another data-center product to its AI infrastructure lineup. … The company is shipping Vera Rubin NVL72 racks through its Data Center Building Block Solutions, combining computing hardware with liquid cooling, networking, storage and power components. The rack design uses 72 Rubin GPUs and 36 Vera CPUs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e182\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Super Micro Computer\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Michael Staiger, Senior Vice President, Super Micro Computer (at a Goldman Sachs conference; reported by GuruFocus)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-09-10\",\n  \"summary\": \"At a Goldman Sachs conference on Sept. 10, Super Micro Computer Senior Vice President Michael Staiger said the company had about $60 billion in orders backing its fiscal 2027 revenue forecast of $65 billion to $72 billion, with demand coming from neocloud operators, enterprises and sovereign customers.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Demand expectations remain tied to AI infrastructure spending. At a Sept. 10 Goldman Sachs conference, Senior Vice President Michael Staiger said the company had about $60 billion in orders backing its fiscal 2027 revenue forecast of $65 billion to $72 billion. The company sees demand from neocloud operators, enterprises and sovereign customers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e183\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (citing NVIDIA's Aug. 26 press release)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-26\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal second-quarter 2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, with Data Center revenue up 117% year over year to $89 billion, according to its Aug. 26, 2026 press release; GAAP gross margin was 75% versus 72.4% a year earlier and GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA's revenue growth has been phenomenal, reaching $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release. … Data Center remained the primary growth engine, with its revenues jumping 117% year over year to $89 billion, indicating continued strength in AI infrastructure demand. … NVIDIA's gross margin reached 75%, up from 72.4% a year ago, while both GAAP and non-GAAP net income increased, demonstrating the company's strong profitability. GAAP operating income more than doubled year over year, underscoring significant operating leverage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e184\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (citing NVIDIA's Aug. 26 press release)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-26\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal third-quarter 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, implying continued sequential growth, and guided a non-GAAP gross margin of 74% for the same quarter.\",\n  \"quote\": \"NVIDIA expects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, indicating continued sequential growth. … In comparison, NVIDIA expects a non-GAAP gross margin of 74% in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, highlighting its much stronger margin profile.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e185\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA Corporation\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA stated that its Vera Rubin platform is now in full production, which the article presents as positioning the company to capitalize on continued AI infrastructure demand.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Profitability is also expected to remain strong, while the company's Vera Rubin platform is now in full production, positioning NVIDIA to capitalize on continued AI infrastructure demand.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e186\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Marvell Technology, Inc.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (citing Marvell's Aug. 27 press release)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-27\",\n  \"summary\": \"Marvell Technology reported record fiscal second-quarter 2027 revenue of $2.739 billion, up 37% year over year, with Data Center revenue growing 46% year over year, according to its Aug. 27, 2026 press release.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Revenues for the fiscal second quarter of 2027 reached a record $2.739 billion, up 37% year over year, according to the company's Aug. 27 press release. With Marvell supplying vital infrastructure for data center systems, its Data Center revenues grew even faster, up 46% year over year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e187\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"Marvell Technology, Inc.\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"Zacks (Marvell management guidance)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"2026-08-27\",\n  \"summary\": \"Marvell Technology management guided fiscal third-quarter 2027 revenue to $3.15 billion, plus or minus 5%, about 15% sequential growth at the midpoint, and remained optimistic about revenue growth through fiscal 2027 and 2028.\",\n  \"quote\": \"For the fiscal third quarter of 2027, management expects revenues to reach $3.15 billion, plus or minus 5%. At the midpoint, it represents roughly 15% sequential growth. Management also remained optimistic about revenue growth throughout fiscal year 2027 and 2028.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e188\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"SpaceX (Elon Musk, CEO)\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com (article via Yahoo Finance)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"On SpaceX's second-quarter earnings call, SpaceX CEO Elon Musk said SpaceX has decided to build exclusively on NVIDIA hardware because he considers the Vera Rubin architecture the best architecture and the best AI computer, citing close cooperation and partnership with NVIDIA; the article characterises this as making SpaceX (which owns xAI and its Grok model) exclusive to NVIDIA.\",\n  \"quote\": \"During SpaceX's second-quarter earnings call, Musk had this to say about SpaceX's relationship with Nvidia: … We've decided to build exclusively on NVIDIA because we think the Vera Rubin architecture is the best architecture. We think it's the best AI computer, and we greatly value our close cooperation and partnership on many levels with NVIDIA. So, we're exclusive to NVIDIA.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e189\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"NVIDIA\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com (article via Yahoo Finance)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported quarterly revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, and converted $63.7 billion of that revenue into operating income, according to the article's summary of its Q2 results.\",\n  \"quote\": \"Nvidia posted an even stronger quarter; revenue was up 106% year over year to $96.2 billion. It converted $63.7 billion of that into operating income, showcasing its impressive profitability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"statement\": \"e190\",\n  \"article_day\": \"2026-09-24\",\n  \"said_by\": \"SpaceX\",\n  \"reported_by\": \"fool.com (article via Yahoo Finance)\",\n  \"original_day\": \"\",\n  \"summary\": \"SpaceX reported second-quarter revenue of $7.8 billion, up 92% year over year, with its AI division revenue up 213% year over year; that AI business is not profitable and had an operating loss of about $143 million, per the article.\",\n  \"quote\": \"During Q2, SpaceX's revenue rose 92% year over year to $7.8 billion. Its AI division showcased particular strength, rising 213% year over year. However, it isn't profitable and had a loss of about $143 million from operations.\"\n }\n]","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/statements-part2.json\\\"; a=json.load(open(p)); [print(x[\\\"statement\\\"], x[\\\"summary\\\"], \\\"QUOTE:\\\", x[\\\"quote\\\"]) for x in a if 110 <= int(x[\\\"statement\\\"][1:]) <= 164]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/statements-part2.json\\\"; a=json.load(open(p)); [print(x[\\\"statement\\\"], x[\\\"summary\\\"], \\\"QUOTE:\\\", x[\\\"quote\\\"]) for x in a if 110 <= int(x[\\\"statement\\\"][1:]) <= 164]'\"","aggregated_output":"e110 NVIDIA reported second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%; Data Center revenue was $89.023 billion, according to the article. QUOTE: Q2 fiscal 2027 delivered revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%. Data Center revenue hit $89.023 billion.\ne111 NVIDIA guided third-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue to $108 billion, a guidance the article says excludes China Data Center compute revenue, cited as geopolitical uncertainty. QUOTE: Management guided Q3 to $108 billion. … Q3 guidance excludes China Data Center compute revenue citing geopolitical uncertainty.\ne112 The article expects NVIDIA's gross margin to bottom at 71% to 72% in Q4 on memory cost inflation and to recover to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale (the item says 'Q4' without naming the fiscal year; context is fiscal 2027). QUOTE: Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.\ne113 The article lists supply commitments of $279 billion among NVIDIA's real risks. QUOTE: Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.\ne114 The article lists guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion among NVIDIA's real risks. QUOTE: Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.\ne115 The article reports that NVIDIA's days sales outstanding (DSO) is extending to 60 days, listing it among the company's real risks. QUOTE: Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.\ne116 Jensen Huang told investors that NVIDIA can supply only 70% of demand, and the article states fiscal 2028 growth is pegged at approximately 70%. QUOTE: Jensen Huang told investors NVIDIA can supply only 70% of demand, with fiscal 2028 growth pegged at approximately 70%.\ne117 The article states that Vera Rubin raises platform value per gigawatt to $40 billion from Blackwell's $25 billion. QUOTE: Vera Rubin ramps platform value per gigawatt from Blackwell's $25 billion to $40 billion.\ne118 The article cites more than $500 billion in third-party AI infrastructure capital being mobilized through NVIDIA partners as one of three catalysts behind its buy call. QUOTE: Three catalysts drive the call: the Vera Rubin production ramp, more than $500 billion in third-party AI infrastructure capital being mobilized through NVIDIA partners, and the opening chapter of physical AI across robotics and autonomous vehicles.\ne119 The article states hyperscaler capex is expected to reach nearly 800 billion in 2026 and 1.3 trillion in 2027. QUOTE: Hyperscaler capex is expected to reach nearly 800 billion in 2026 and 1.3 trillion in 2027, a wave that also pulls in the power, cooling, and networking suppliers we profiled in a free report on seven AI infrastructure names that aren't chipmakers.\ne120 Advanced Micro Devices posted second-quarter fiscal 2026 revenue of $11.536 billion, up 50.11%, with Data Center revenue up 107%, according to the article. QUOTE: Advanced Micro Devices ( NASDAQ:AMD ) posted Q2 fiscal 2026 revenue of $11.536 billion, up 50.11%, with Data Center up 107%.\ne121 Broadcom competes in custom AI ASICs and networking; its third-quarter fiscal 2026 revenue reached $29.591 billion, up 85.5%, with AI semiconductor revenue of $16.70 billion growing 221% year over year, according to the article. QUOTE: Broadcom ( NASDAQ:AVGO ) competes in custom AI ASICs and networking. Q3 fiscal 2026 revenue reached $29.591 billion, up 85.5%, with AI semiconductor revenue of $16.70 billion growing 221% year over year.\ne122 NVIDIA's second-quarter net income rose 126% year-on-year to $59.7bn, according to the Yahoo Finance UK article, which notes earnings grew roughly 4.5 times faster than the share price over the same comparison. QUOTE: Second-quarter net income rocketed 126% to $59.7bn year-on-year, around 4.5 times faster than the stock.\ne123 On 21 September 2026, autonomous-freight operator Einride AB (NASDAQ: ENRD) announced a strategic collaboration with NVIDIA around NVIDIA's DRIVE Hyperion autonomous-driving compute platform, according to this 23 September 2026 article; no financial terms, volumes or contract value were disclosed, and the article notes Einride's separate fleet plan (about 500 Tesla Semis, part of a roughly 1,500–2,000-vehicle fleet by 2028) is distinct from the NVIDIA tie-up. QUOTE: On September 21, the autonomous-freight operator announced a strategic collaboration with NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) around DRIVE Hyperion, while its separate fleet plan calls for hundreds of Tesla, Inc. (NASDAQ: TSLA ) Semis. … Nvidia's Hyperion platform gives Einride a standardized path for perception and autonomous-driving compute.\ne124 NVIDIA mentioned warm-water cooling technology during a keynote address, and investors read the remark as a threat to SPX Technologies' air-cooled cooling towers; the article ties that reading to the selloff that has dragged SPX shares from above $230 toward their 52-week low. The item gives no date, product name or technical detail for the NVIDIA remark. QUOTE: The selloff that has dragged the stock from above $230 down toward its 52-week low has a specific, nameable cause. … Nvidia mentioned warm-water cooling technology during a keynote, and investors immediately read that as a threat to SPX's air-cooled towers.\ne125 SPX Technologies lifted its data center capacity expectations to $1.1 billion from $750 million — a 47% increase — which the article says reflects real customer commitments rather than forward-looking optimism; the raise was disclosed alongside its Q2 2026 results (revenue of $679 million, adjusted EPS of $2.02 versus a $1.85 estimate, and full-year adjusted EPS guidance raised to $8.20–$8.60). QUOTE: The company also lifted its data center capacity expectations to $1.1B from $750M, a 47% increase that reflects real customer commitments rather than forward-looking optimism.\ne126 Motley Fool contributor Jeremy Bowman reports that Wall Street expects Nvidia to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year, contrasting that pace with the S&P 500's slower growth. QUOTE: Because of its central position in the AI boom, Nvidia is growing much faster than the S&P 500. Wall Street expects the company to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year.\ne127 Motley Fool contributor Jeremy Bowman reports that Nvidia is expected by consensus to earn earnings per share of $15.68 in fiscal 2028, which ends in January of that year. QUOTE: For fiscal 2028, which ends in January of that year, Nvidia is expected to have earnings per share of $15.68.\ne128 Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter (quarter ended July 26, 2026) revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and an acceleration from the previous quarter, with the data center business contributing all but about $7 billion of the total; net income rose 126% year over year to $59.7 billion. QUOTE: Nvidia's fiscal 2027 second quarter (ended July 26) was another exceptional one. Revenue grew 106% year over year to $96.2 billion, an acceleration from the previous quarter, and the data center business contributed all but about $7 billion of the total. Profit kept up. Net income rose 126% year over year, to $59.7 billion.\ne129 Nvidia management guided revenue for the current quarter (fiscal Q3 2027) to $108.0 billion, described in the item as another step up from fiscal Q2's $96.2 billion. QUOTE: And management guided for another step up in this quarter (fiscal Q3): $108.0 billion of revenue.\ne130 On Nvidia's earnings call in late August 2026, chief financial officer Colette Kress guided fiscal 2028 revenue growth of approximately 70%, characterising the outlook as supply-constrained. QUOTE: On the company's earnings call in late August, chief financial officer Colette Kress went a whole year further. … \"We expect to grow revenue by approximately 70% in fiscal 2028,\" Kress said. \"This is a supply-constrained outlook.\"\ne131 AMD reported second-quarter 2026 revenue of a record $11.5 billion, up 50% from a year earlier; its data center segment, which sells EPYC server processors and Instinct GPUs into the same AI build-out Nvidia serves, more than doubled year over year to $6.7 billion, or 58% of company revenue. QUOTE: AMD's rally has real results behind it. Revenue for the second quarter of 2026 hit a record $11.5 billion, up 50% from a year ago. … And the data center segment, which sells EPYC server processors and Instinct graphics processing units into the same AI build-out Nvidia serves, more than doubled year over year, totaling $6.7 billion (58% of the company's revenue).\ne132 AMD guided third-quarter 2026 revenue to around $13 billion, which the item says implies about 41% year-over-year growth. QUOTE: Guidance for the third quarter of 2026 is around $13 billion, which implies about 41% year-over-year growth.\ne133 AMD chief executive Lisa Su told analysts on the company's August 2026 earnings call that AMD now expects data center segment revenue to more than double year over year in 2027. QUOTE: And CEO Lisa Su told analysts on the company's August earnings call that the bigger move happens next year. … \"[W]e now expect data center segment revenue to more than double year-over-year in 2027,\" Su said.\ne134 NVIDIA's reported Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with Q3 fiscal 2027 revenue guided to $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%; the article uses this to argue the insider sales reflect portfolio moves, not a business warning. QUOTE: Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue was $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year, with a Q3 guide of $108 billion at the midpoint and a preliminary fiscal 2028 growth expectation of approximately 70%. … Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year to $96B, making the director's trim a portfolio move, not a business warning.\ne135 NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in the Frontier AI Labs and helped arrange over $500 billion of third-party capital with six infrastructure providers, and CEO Jensen Huang acknowledged the scale of that support while saying the company does not see it as 'circular financing'. QUOTE: The louder concern is circular financing. NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in the Frontier AI Labs and helped arrange over $500 billion of third-party capital with six infrastructure providers. CEO Jensen Huang addressed the skepticism directly: \"We recognize the scale of this support, and we know some will call this circular financing. We see it differently.\"\ne136 The article reports that NVIDIA's supply commitments have surged to $279 billion and its guarantee obligations are capped at $108.5 billion, describing both as real balance-sheet exposures if demand slips. QUOTE: Bear: the sale is large, outside a prearranged plan, and arrives as the market questions whether the spending cycle is self-funded. Supply commitments surged to $279 billion, and guarantee obligations are capped at $108.5 billion. Those are real balance-sheet exposures if demand slips.\ne137 NVIDIA reported $96.2 billion in revenue for its fiscal second quarter, up 106% from the same period a year earlier, and a 75% gross margin. QUOTE: Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year. … The company also produced a 75% gross margin\ne138 NVIDIA management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year. QUOTE: management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year\ne139 NVIDIA guided to $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth. QUOTE: Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.\ne140 The article reports that NVIDIA's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months, with receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July. QUOTE: However, a closer look at the company's balance sheet shows that Nvidia's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months. … A big part of that is the company's receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July.\ne141 The article calculates that NVIDIA's days sales outstanding rose from 45 to 60 days in one quarter, which it says means customers are taking longer to pay. QUOTE: Nvidia's DSO went from 45 to 60 days in one quarter. Customers are taking longer to pay.\ne142 NVIDIA said it extended payment terms on large orders from certain customers, which the article cites as the reason for the rise in days sales outstanding. QUOTE: To be fair, Nvidia told us why. The company extended payment terms on large orders from certain customers.\ne143 NVIDIA agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of data center lease obligations for OpenAI. QUOTE: For example, Nvidia agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of data center lease obligations for OpenAI.\ne144 NVIDIA has formed partnerships to raise over $500 billion of outside capital for AI infrastructure, according to the article. QUOTE: It has formed partnerships to raise over $500 billion of outside capital for AI infrastructure.\ne145 IonQ announced it will deploy its Superion 256 quantum computer on-premise at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center. The article describes the deployment as tying IonQ's Superion 256 hardware to CUDA Q and GB200 NVL72 infrastructure in an on-premise environment — a partner integration with NVIDIA's Blackwell-generation systems and quantum software platform; no shipment date, order value or scale of NVIDIA benefit is given. QUOTE: IonQ recently announced it will deploy its Superion 256 quantum computer on-premise at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, while also unveiling an end-to-end real-time quantum error correction decoder that runs on a single off-the-shelf CPU with minimal computational delay. … The NVIDIA Accelerated Quantum Research Center deployment stands out as the most relevant announcement here, because it ties IonQ's Superion 256 hardware to CUDA Q and GB200 NVL72 infrastructure in a real on premise environment.\ne146 Apple is making an unusually aggressive push into enterprise artificial intelligence, pitching its newest high-end Macs — upgraded Mac mini and Mac Studio systems — as an alternative to the expensive cloud computing capacity that has helped Nvidia and Microsoft dominate the AI boom, arguing businesses can run AI workloads locally rather than paying cloud providers for tokens. The item gives no adoption, order or spending figures for the effort. QUOTE: Apple ( NASDAQ:AAPL ) is making an unusually aggressive push into enterprise artificial intelligence , pitching its newest high-end Macs as an alternative to the expensive cloud infrastructure that has helped Nvidia ( NASDAQ:NVDA ) and Microsoft ( NASDAQ:MSFT ) dominate the AI boom. … Its upgraded Mac mini and Mac Studio systems are aimed at tasks including software development and complex business workflows.\ne147 IonQ announced that its Superion 256 trapped-ion quantum system will be installed in Nvidia's accelerated quantum research center, where it will run as a niche processing system alongside Nvidia GPU clusters — a deployment IonQ disclosed alongside its decoder breakthrough. QUOTE: In addition to that news, IonQ announced a potentially important step toward commercializing its quantum systems. Its Superion 256 system will be installed in Nvidia's accelerated quantum research center to run as a niche processing system alongside Nvidia GPU (graphics processing unit) clusters.\ne148 The article reports that Washington has for years restricted China's access to Nvidia's most advanced AI chips and to the equipment used to make them, on the bet that limiting computing power would keep Chinese AI a generation behind; the restriction is described as in force as of the 23 September 2026 article. QUOTE: Washington has for years restricted China's access to Nvidia's most advanced AI chips and the equipment to make them, betting that starving computing power would keep Chinese AI a generation behind.\ne149 During the September 2026 Trump–Xi state visit, the article said neither side appeared ready to put chip export controls on the table; Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and U.S. Trade Representative Jamieson Greer met Vice Premier He Lifeng in New York over the weekend and set up a formal AI channel for incident warnings, and Greer said explicitly that export controls on advanced chips and chipmaking equipment were not on the agenda. QUOTE: As Trump hosts Xi for a multi-day state visit, neither side appears ready to put chip export controls on the table. … Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and U.S. Trade Representative Jamieson Greer met Vice Premier He Lifeng in New York over the weekend and set up a formal AI channel for incident warnings. But Greer said explicitly that export controls on advanced chips and chipmaking equipment were not on the agenda.\ne150 Huawei said at its annual Huawei Connect conference, the week before the 23 September 2026 article, that its Ascent 960DT AI chip will ship in the first quarter of 2027, three quarters ahead of its original schedule. QUOTE: At its annual Huawei Connect conference last week, Huawei said its Ascent 960DT will ship in the first quarter of 2027 , three quarters ahead of its original schedule.\ne151 At the Apsara Conference in Hangzhou on the Tuesday before the 23 September 2026 article, Alibaba's chip unit unveiled the Zhenwu V900 AI chip, which it says triples the performance of its predecessor and will go on sale in early 2027. QUOTE: At the Apsara Conference in Hangzhou on Tuesday, Alibaba's chip unit unveiled the Zhenwu V900 chip , which triples the performance of its predecessor and will go on sale in early 2027.\ne152 The article reports that Huawei's latest SuperPoD computing architecture links far fewer processors than originally planned, and that each Huawei chip still delivers roughly half the compute of Nvidia's chips. QUOTE: But the approach has limits. Huawei's latest SuperPoD computing architecture links far fewer processors than originally planned, and each chip still delivers roughly half the compute of Nvidia's.\ne153 Huawei Chairman Eric Xu acknowledged that Huawei may not be able to make enough AI chips to meet Chinese domestic demand, and that Chinese AI developers may not be advanced enough to experience rogue safety risks, as reported in the 23 September 2026 article. QUOTE: Chairman Eric Xu acknowledged that Huawei may not be able to make enough chips to meet domestic demand, and that Chinese AI developers may not be advanced enough to experience rogue safety risks.\ne154 Chris Miller, a Tufts University professor and author of 'Chip War', said Chinese firms remain substantially short of the chips needed to train and deploy advanced models and rely heavily on smuggling chips or gaining access to data centers outside China, concluding that China is still highly dependent on the U.S. for advanced chips. QUOTE: Chinese firms remain substantially short of the chips needed to train and deploy advanced models, and rely heavily on smuggling chips or gaining access to data centers outside China, Miller said. \"China is still highly dependent on the U.S. for advanced chips.\"\ne155 DeepSeek, the AI startup whose low-cost model rattled global markets the previous year, reportedly lined up the largest known cluster of Huawei chips built to date, according to the article. QUOTE: DeepSeek, the startup whose low-cost model rattled global markets last year, reportedly lined up the largest known cluster of Huawei chips built to date.\ne156 IonQ announced on 23 September 2026 a partnership with Nvidia to deploy IonQ's trapped-ion quantum computer at Nvidia's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, aligning IonQ's next-generation trapped-ion architecture with Nvidia's CUDA-Q open platform and H200 GPUs so researchers can run hybrid classical-quantum workflows. The item reports the announcement as news; no contract value, capacity or shipment volume is given. QUOTE: IonQ (IONQ) shares inched higher on Sept. 23 after announcing a landmark partnership with Nvidia (NVDA) to deploy its quantum computer at the AI titan's Accelerated Quantum Research Center. … The deal aligns IonQ's trapped-ion hardware with Nvidia's CUDA-Q platform, advancing hybrid classical-quantum supercomputing. … Integrating IonQ's next-generation trapped-ion architecture with Nvidia's CUDA-Q open platform and H200 GPUs allows researchers to run accelerated hybrid workflows and generative AI circuit optimization.\ne157 NVIDIA Enterprise Sales Director for Latin America Marcio Gomes said that 82 Mexican startups are participating in NVIDIA Inception, the chipmaker's free global program that gives AI startups technical training, developer tools, preferred pricing on selected hardware and software, cloud credits and investor introductions, with no application or membership fees and no equity requirements. The item gives no fee revenue, order, capacity or spending figure tied to the program and no date for the count. QUOTE: Mexico has 82 startups participating in NVIDIA Inception, the chipmaker’s global program designed to support artificial intelligence companies through technical resources, business guidance, and connections to investors. The figure, confirmed by Marcio Gomes, Enterprise Sales Director for Latin America, NVIDIA, highlights the growing presence of AI-focused businesses within Mexico’s technology ecosystem.\ne158 Nvidia-backed startup Skild AI, together with Nvidia and contract manufacturer Foxconn, recently began using Skild's 'Skild Brain' omni-bodied foundation model on dual-arm robots at an Nvidia factory in Houston to assemble Nvidia Blackwell GPU systems — a deployment the article presents as under way, built on Nvidia AI infrastructure (Cosmos, Isaac Lab, Isaac Sim and Omniverse) for data generation, training, simulation and deployment. QUOTE: The technology is already being deployed at an Nvidia factory in Houston, where Skild, Nvidia and contract electronics manufacturing giant Foxconn recently began using the Skild Brain omni-bodied foundation model on dual-arm robots to assemble Nvidia Blackwell GPU systems. … S1 was built on Nvidia AI infrastructure, using Cosmos, Isaac Lab, Isaac Sim and Omniverse across data generation, training, simulation and deployment.\ne159 Skild AI, the Nvidia-backed developer of a general-purpose robot foundation model, said it reached a $100 million annual revenue run rate earlier in September 2026, only 10 months after its first commercial deployment; the company cited this as evidence that robot foundation models are moving beyond demos into real work. QUOTE: Skild reached a $100 million annual revenue run rate earlier this month, just 10 months after its first commercial deployment. This, according to the company, is evidence that robot foundation models are moving beyond demos and into real work.\ne160 IonQ said on Wednesday (23 September 2026) that its Superion 256 quantum system is scheduled to be installed next year at Nvidia's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, where it will be linked directly to an Nvidia GB200 NVL72 system, using Nvidia's NVQLink technology and CUDA-Q platform to connect the quantum processor to Nvidia's accelerated computing infrastructure; the joint research program will focus on hybrid quantum-classical software and large-scale system prototypes. IonQ described the system as the first on-premises quantum processor deployed at the center. This is a stated deployment plan for 2027, not a confirmed order, delivery or revenue for Nvidia. QUOTE: IonQ (IONQ) shares jumped in pre-market trade on Wednesday after the company said it successfully tested its first real-time quantum error decoder and announced that its Superion 256 system will become the first on-premises quantum processor deployed at Nvidia’s Accelerated Quantum Research Center. … IonQ said on Wednesday that its Superion 256 will be installed at Nvidia’s Accelerated Quantum Research Center next year, where it will be linked directly to an Nvidia GB200 NVL72 system. … The companies will use Nvidia’s NVQLink technology and CUDA-Q platform to connect the quantum processor with Nvidia’s accelerated computing infrastructure. The research program will focus on hybrid quantum-classical software and large-scale system prototypes.\ne161 IonQ announced that its sixth-generation Superion 256 trapped-ion quantum processing unit (QPU) will be the first on-premise quantum computer installed at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC), scheduled for installation in 2027 alongside IonQ's first commercial deliveries. The deployment establishes a direct hardware interconnect between IonQ's 256-qubit system and an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 accelerated computing rack via NVIDIA NVQLink, with hybrid quantum-classical workloads on the unified system orchestrated by NVIDIA's open-source CUDA-Q software platform. QUOTE: Trapped-ion quantum hardware developer IonQ (NYSE: IONQ) has announced that its sixth-generation Superion 256 quantum processing unit (QPU) will serve as the first on-premise quantum computer installed at the NVIDIA Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC) . Scheduled for installation in 2027 alongside first commercial deliveries, the deployment establishes a direct hardware interconnect between IonQ’s 256-qubit system and an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 accelerated computing rack via NVIDIA NVQLink . Hybrid quantum-classical workloads across the unified system will be orchestrated by the open-source NVIDIA CUDA-Q software platform.\ne162 On NVIDIA's most recent earnings call, the company said data center capital expenditures by the big five AI hyperscalers will approach $800 billion this year (2026) and are estimated to rise to $1.3 trillion next year (2027), as reported by The Motley Fool. QUOTE: During its most recent earnings call, Nvidia noted that this year's data center capital expenditures from the big five AI hyperscalers will approach $800 billion. Next year, that figure is estimated to rise to $1.3 trillion.\ne163 NVIDIA said it sees global annual data center capital expenditures increasing to $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030, a long-dated demand forecast quoted by The Motley Fool. QUOTE: Ultimately, Nvidia sees global annual data center capital expenditures increasing to $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\ne164 TSMC announced an additional $100 billion investment in its Arizona production facilities during Q2, an expansion reported by The Motley Fool as a sign the foundry expects more demand requiring additional production capacity; the item does not state the build-out schedule or any allocation of that capacity to NVIDIA. QUOTE: Furthermore, TSMC announced an additional $100 billion investment in its Arizona production facilities during Q2, so clearly it sees more demand coming that requires increased production capacity.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"statement\":\"e96\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e97\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e98\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e99\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e100\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e101\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e102\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e103\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":\"The nearly $800 billion estimate directly supports the $775 billion to $825 billion answer for 2026.\",\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e104\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e105\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e106\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e107\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e108\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e109\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e110\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e111\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"Excluding China data-center compute revenue because of geopolitical uncertainty makes timely Blackwell authorization and Chinese permission less likely.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e112\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e113\",\"v1\":\"The quoted $108.5 billion guarantee cap makes a disclosure of $100 billion or more more likely, though the covered obligations may differ.\",\"v2\":\"The reported $279 billion supply commitments make a disclosure of $200 billion or more more likely.\",\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e114\",\"v1\":\"The reported $108.5 billion guarantee cap makes a disclosure of $100 billion or more more likely, though the covered obligations may differ.\",\"v2\":\"The quoted $279 billion supply commitments make a disclosure of $200 billion or more more likely.\",\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e115\",\"v1\":\"The quoted $108.5 billion guarantee cap makes a disclosure of $100 billion or more more likely, though the covered obligations may differ.\",\"v2\":\"The quoted $279 billion supply commitments make a disclosure of $200 billion or more more likely.\",\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e116\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e117\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e118\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"The cited Vera Rubin production ramp makes volume shipments and first revenue by fiscal year-end more likely.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e119\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":\"Expected 2026 hyperscaler capex near $800 billion supports the $775 billion to $825 billion answer, subject to the spending scope matching.\",\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e120\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e121\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e122\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e123\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e124\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e125\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e126\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e127\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e128\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e129\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e130\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e131\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e132\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e133\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e134\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e135\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e136\",\"v1\":\"The reported $108.5 billion guarantee cap makes a disclosure of $100 billion or more more likely, though the covered obligations may differ.\",\"v2\":\"Reported supply commitments of $279 billion make a disclosure of $200 billion or more more likely.\",\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e137\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e138\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e139\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e140\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e141\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e142\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e143\",\"v1\":\"The reported guarantee of up to $105 billion for OpenAI leases makes a $100 billion-or-more disclosure more likely.\",\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e144\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e145\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e146\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e147\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e148\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"Washington's continuing restrictions on advanced Nvidia chips make U.S. authorization for Blackwell by January less likely.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e149\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"Advanced-chip export controls were excluded from the leaders' talks, making a negotiated opening for Blackwell sales by January less likely.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e150\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"Huawei's accelerated domestic chip launch could reduce China's need to permit Blackwell imports, making joint approval less likely.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":\"Huawei's accelerated domestic chip launch could reduce pressure on MIIT to approve Nvidia purchases, making approval less likely.\"}\n{\"statement\":\"e151\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"Alibaba's planned domestic AI chip could reduce China's need for Blackwell imports, making joint approval less likely.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":\"Alibaba's planned domestic AI chip could reduce pressure for approval of its Nvidia purchase, making MIIT approval less likely.\"}\n{\"statement\":\"e152\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"Huawei's weaker chips and constrained system scale increase the value of Nvidia imports, making Chinese permission for Blackwell more plausible.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":\"Huawei's weaker chips and constrained system scale increase the value of Nvidia alternatives, making MIIT purchase approval more plausible.\"}\n{\"statement\":\"e153\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"Huawei's possible domestic supply shortfall increases pressure for imported chips, making Chinese permission for Blackwell more plausible.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":\"Huawei's possible domestic supply shortfall increases pressure for alternatives, making MIIT approval of Nvidia purchases more plausible.\"}\n{\"statement\":\"e154\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":\"Chinese firms' shortage of advanced chips increases the incentive to permit Blackwell imports, making joint approval more plausible.\",\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":\"Chinese firms' advanced-chip shortage increases demand for alternatives, making MIIT approval of Nvidia purchases more plausible.\"}\n{\"statement\":\"e155\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e156\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e157\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e158\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e159\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e160\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e161\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e162\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":\"Nvidia's estimate that big-five 2026 data-center capex approaches $800 billion supports the $775 billion to $825 billion answer.\",\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e163\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e164\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e165\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e166\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e167\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e168\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"Vera Rubin is in full production, making volume shipments and first revenue by fiscal year-end more likely.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e169\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e170\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"The expected Vera Rubin ramp supports eventual shipments, but its timing is unspecified, so it only modestly favors completion by fiscal year-end.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e171\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e172\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e173\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e174\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e175\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e176\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e177\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e178\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e179\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e180\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e181\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"Super Micro is shipping Vera Rubin racks commercially, making Nvidia's volume shipments and first revenue by fiscal year-end more likely.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e182\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e183\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e184\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e185\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"Vera Rubin is in full production, making volume shipments and first revenue by fiscal year-end more likely.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e186\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e187\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e188\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":\"SpaceX's decision to build on Nvidia and its preference for Vera Rubin support customer demand, making volume shipments more likely.\",\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e189\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}\n{\"statement\":\"e190\",\"v1\":null,\"v2\":null,\"v3\":null,\"v4\":null,\"v5\":null,\"v6\":null,\"v7\":null}"}}
